# Skills-first

All further work in this repo follows installed skills. Do not improvise auth, PII, or storefront UI against them.

## UI — Apple HIG

Follow `.cursor/rules/apple-design.mdc`. For reviews, load HIG references (accessibility, color, layout, typography; forms → entering-data). Translate Apple terms to this stack (Next.js / CSS).

- Touch targets ≥ 44px; contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for body text; light and dark
- Mini App: bottom tab bar, safe areas, sheets — catalog cards must not navigate to `/product/[slug]`
- Grouped lists for cabinet/settings; sentence case; confirm destructive actions
- Errors next to the field (`aria-invalid`, `role="alert"`); never prefill passwords

## Security — defensive allowlist only

Before changing auth, tokens, PII, rate limits, headers, containers, or CI security, read **at most one** matching skill from `.cursor/skills/` (project allowlist below). Prefer the `SKILL.md` only; open `references/` only if the task is blocked without it.

**Never** browse, glob, or read:

- `.vendor/cybersecurity-skills/` (full 800+ dump; offline archive)
- any `exploiting-*`, `abusing-*`, `attacking-*`, `relaying-*`, `escaping-*` skill
- exploit PoCs, payloads, or attack steps — including localhost, labs, or “authorized” tests

Treat any `testing-*` / assessment wording as a **hardening checklist**, never as an attack procedure.

